cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or build upon these proofs, certificates, or constructions, please cite this work as below."
type: software
title: "Machine-Verified Two-Sided Bounds for Simple Multi-Item Auctions: 2.1946 <= c* <= 2.486 and an i.i.d. Lower Bound above 1.316"
authors:
  - family-names: "Sievert"
    given-names: "Max"
    email: "sievert-max@gmx.de"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Maxkxkxk/simple-auctions-lean4"
url: "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.24482558"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.24482558"
date-released: 2026-11-23
version: "1.0.1"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - mechanism design
  - multi-item auctions
  - algorithmic game theory
  - Lean 4
  - formal verification
  - simple auctions
  - separate selling
  - grand bundling
abstract: >-
  Complete Lean 4 formal proofs (zero sorry, zero native_decide, standard axioms only)
  and exact rational Python certificates establishing: (1) a general lower bound
  REV(D) > 2.1946 * max(SREV(D), BREV(D)); (2) a universal upper bound
  REV(D) <= 1.1187 * SREV(D) + 1.367299 * BREV(D) <= 2.486 * max(SREV(D), BREV(D))
  for all finite independent product distributions; (3) the combined bracket
  2.1946 <= c* <= 2.486; and (4) a 40-item i.i.d. lower bound
  REV(F^{otimes 40}) > 1.316 * max(SREV, BREV) (with exact rational verification
  >= 1.324907 for 100 i.i.d. items).
